  "id": "roessler-chaos-attractor-phy",
  "name": "Roessler Chaos Attractor",
  "description": "The Rossler attractor is a system of three non-linear ordinary differential equations originally studied by Otto Rossler (1976). It was designed to be simpler than the Lorenz attractor while still exhibiting chaotic dynamics. The system shows period-doubling bifurcation route to chaos. Reference: Lorenz, E. N. (1963). Deterministic nonperiodic flow. Journal of the Atmospheric Sciences, 20(2), 130-141. DOI: https://doi.org/10.1175/1520-0469(1963)020<0130:DNF>2.0.CO;2",
  "source": "https://doi.org/10.1016/0375-9601(76)90101-8",
  "reference": "Rossler OE. An equation for continuous chaos. Physics Letters A. 1976;57(5):397-398.",
